/name/ ignores a folder named name at the project root. name/ can match that folder at any level
.
*.tmp ignores files ending in .tmp, like notes.tmp. *. would match names that end with a dot, so use the full extension.
.name matches a file literally named .name. 
The starting dot often marks a hidden file, but Git doesn’t automatically treat every dotfile as junk. For example,
 .gitignore and .editorconfig are useful files.


!name can allow a matching file back if an earlier rule ignored it. !keep.tmp allows keep.tmp even if an earlier rule ignores it;
 then use git add keep.tmp.

# Compiled bytecode
*.class

# IntelliJ project files
.idea/
*.iml

# Build output folders (javac/IntelliJ default output)
out/
bin/
target/

# Local learning plan
/java-master-sheet.md

# OS junk
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
